Setting up CUDA C++
I'm pulling together a CUDA C++ code skeleton for the GTX560, covering headers, streams, events, and cuBLAS calls, with a prototype pipeline for benchmarking. Awesome—here’s a minimal, self‑contained CUDA/C++ skeleton you can use to prototype the GTX 560 (Fermi, CC 2.1) pipeline. It shows:

headers & error‑checking
stream & event setup
cuBLAS GEMM call (FP32)
a reference qmm_kernel signature (quantized matmul stub)
simple bias add kernel
pinned host memory & async H2D/D2H transfers
a triple‑buffered stream pipeline


Assumptions (Fermi/CUDA‑8 era mindset):
• FP32 math via cuBLAS cublasSgemm (no Tensor Cores/WMMA; DP4A not available on Fermi).
• Column‑major layout for cuBLAS. Shapes: X (M×K), W (K×N), Y (M×N).
• Keep W resident on device; stream X and Y via pinned memory + async copies.
• Triple buffering with 4 streams: H2D, GEMM, Bias, D2H.




main.cu (minimal skeleton)
// nvcc -arch=sm_21 -std=c++11 -lcublas main.cu -o prototype
// Tested syntax against CUDA 8.0-era expectations (keep C++11; avoid newer dialects).

#include <cstdio>
#include <cstdlib>
#include <vector>
#include <cassert>
#include <cuda_runtime.h>
#include <cublas_v2.h>

// ---------------------------------------------
// Error checking helpers
// ---------------------------------------------
#define CHECK_CUDA(call) do { \n  cudaError_t _e = (call); \n  if (_e != cudaSuccess) { \n    fprintf(stderr, "CUDA error %s:%d: %s
", __FILE__, __LINE__, cudaGetErrorString(_e)); \n    std::exit(EXIT_FAILURE); \n  } \n} while(0)

#define CHECK_CUBLAS(call) do { \n  cublasStatus_t _s = (call); \n  if (_s != CUBLAS_STATUS_SUCCESS) { \n    fprintf(stderr, "cuBLAS error %s:%d: status=%d
", __FILE__, __LINE__, int(_s)); \n    std::exit(EXIT_FAILURE); \n  } \n} while(0)

// ---------------------------------------------
// Minimal bias-add kernel (Y += b row-wise)
// Y is MxN column-major; b is length N
// ---------------------------------------------
__global__ void add_bias_kernel(float* __restrict__ Y,
                                const float* __restrict__ b,
                                int M, int N) {
  int col = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;
  if (col >= N) return;
  // column-major: each column is contiguous in memory stepping by M
  for (int row = 0; row < M; ++row) {
    Y[col * M + row] += b[col];
  }
}

